}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Lord of Ruin Jagando Jr.''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Jagando is a powerful [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|anti-Traitless unit]], combining both damage and crowd-control through his strong and knockback abilities with his decent range, especially when paired with other crowd-control units like [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Crystal Cat]], [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]], [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist Cat]] and other anti-Traitless Cats, providing the bulk of your DPS while they ward threats from him. Jagando Jr.'s generalist value is lacking, and while he can be used as a DPS unit, there are usually better, more accessible options. Fortunately, his guaranteed Surge Attack can serve as a helpful multiplier, dealing a total of 36,720 damage to Traitless enemies, if not double when they are hit by the Surge.

Jagando Jr.'s Surge and Curse immunities are nothing to dismiss, either, making him a prime choice for stages like [[Heavenly Tower]] [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 50|Floor 50]] and [[Flow Like the Stream (Merciless)|Flow Like the Stream]], even if his Curse Immunity is not as handy as Surge Immunity. Topping this all off, Jagando Jr. is guaranteed to inflict Knockback on his third hit, ensuring that any [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless enemies]] are pushed back for his safety and shutting down nasty Traitless pushers like [[R.Ost]] for good. His Surge can even hit them for a second knockback, being able to sometimes pierce further and hit enemies outside of his range. He's a prime choice for {{4c}} stages involving Traitless enemies that he outranges, and helps synergize and defend your other [[:Category:Special Cats|Special]] and [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare]] DPS units, serving well in the {{4c}} difficulties of the [[The Noble Tribe]], [[Procrastinator Parade]], [[No Return Flights]], and more.

To summarize, Jagando Jr. is basically a free [[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST]] unit, holding similar levels of anti-Traitless power.

