==Trivia==
*The name Jagando (ジャガンドー) may be derived from 邪 ''ja'' (evil), ジャガーノート ''jagānōto'' (juggernaut) and シドー ''Shidō'' (the Japanese name of [[wikia:dragonquest:Malroth|Malroth]] from ''[[wikipedia:Dragon Quest|Dragon Quest]]'').
*Jagando Jr. may have been inspired by the Hindu god of destruction, [[wikipedia:Shiva|Shiva]], who is often depicted with multiple pairs of arms and [https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:6_Śiva_and_Pārvatī_seated_on_a_terrace._1800_(circa)_BM.jpg blue skin] like [[Lord of Ruin Jagando]]. Shiva's ''[[wikipedia:Vahana|vāhana]]'', [[wikipedia:Nandi (Hinduism)|Nandi]], is a bull, which may be referenced by the horns on Jagando Jr.'s head. The skulls on Jagando Jr.'s body could be based on the [[wikipedia:Mundamala|Mundamala]] (skull garland) worn by Shiva, and Jagando Jr. being dropped from [[Mount Aku (Aku Realm)|Mount Aku]] could be a reference to how Shiva resides on the mountain [[wikipedia:Kailasha|Kailasha]], where he meditates sitting in a lotus position, the same pose as the [[Media:Bg137.png|cat statue]] in the non-[[Mount Aku (Aku Realm)/Invasion|invaded]] version of Mount Aku.
*[[The Aku Realms]]' ending mentions that the egg Jagando Jr. hatched from was spit out by Lord of Ruin Jagando upon his defeat. This is a reference to [[wikia:dragonball:King Piccolo|King Piccolo]] from ''[[wikipedia:Dragon Ball|Dragon Ball]]'', whose last action before dying was to spit out an egg containing his final child and incarnation, [[wikia:dragonball:Piccolo|Piccolo Jr]].
*Jagando Jr. is the first [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cat]] who is confirmed to be a separate entity from his antagonistic counterpart.

